<%# == Where this run's wall clock went, by spec file
        The other half of the question the panel above answers, off the same rows of the same run,
        and NOT derivable from it. That ranking is by INDIVIDUAL cost and ten rows long: on a
        20,000-example suite it shows 0.05% of the run, and a file holding four hundred examples at
        fifty milliseconds each is twenty seconds of wall clock with every one of its rows far
        below the head. Outliers and concentration are different questions and this panel asks the
        second one.

        Grouped on the INCLUDING file (`spec_file_path`), so a shared example group's time lands on
        the file that ran it rather than on a `spec/support/` helper that ran nothing — the rule
        `SpecObservation`'s class comment states and spec/requests/api/v1/ingest_spec.rb pins
        end-to-end.

        By FILE, and the panel below this one takes the same rows up to the DIRECTORY. Two rungs,
        two reads, neither derived from the other: a by-file top ten shows ten files, and a
        directory holding forty files at two seconds each outweighs every one of them without
        appearing here at all. Both narrow on `test_run_id` and group on top of that index, so
        neither needed an index of its own — the `text_pattern_ops` index this comment once said a
        subtree rollup was waiting on governs a prefix PREDICATE, and a whole-run rollup has none
        to serve (EXPLAIN-certified in spec/models/spec_observation_spec.rb).

        ONE run, like the panel above, and for the same reason: `example_id` is positional and not
        stable across refactors, so anything spanning runs would be comparing rows not known to be
        the same tests.

        Same visibility rule as the panel above — rendered when the run WROTE example rows, and a
        run with rows but no timings renders and says so. Outside the `manage_keys` gate: read-only
        suite telemetry, nothing credential and nothing actionable. %>
<% if @spec_file_durations&.recorded? %>
      <%= render UI::PanelComponent.new(title: "Heaviest spec files", id: "spec-file-durations") do %>
        <% if @spec_file_durations.layer? && @spec_file_durations.rows.empty? %>
          <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "spec-file-durations-basis") do %>
            No example of this run declared <code><%= @spec_file_durations.layer %></code> as its layer, so
            there is no spec file to rank by that layer's time. The layer is what each example's
            <code>@intent</code> declared, never inferred from the path.
          <% end %>
          <p class="text-xs" id="spec-file-durations-clear-layer">
            <%= link_to "Clear layer filter",
                        drill_down_path(@repository, layer: nil, anchor: "spec-file-durations"),
                        class: "rc-link" %>
          </p>
        <% elsif @spec_file_durations.any_timed? %>
          <%= render UI::NoteComponent.new(summary: "How to read this", id: "spec-file-durations-basis") do %>
            <% if @spec_file_durations.truncated? %>
              The <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_durations.rows.size) %> heaviest of the
              <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_durations.file_count) %> files the run named
              above recorded, heaviest first
            <% else %>
              All <%= number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_durations.file_count) %>
              <%= "file".pluralize(@spec_file_durations.file_count) %> the run named above
              recorded, heaviest first
            <% end %>
            — every example's duration summed onto the file that ran it, so a shared example group
            counts against the file including it rather than against the helper defining it.
            <% if @spec_file_durations.layer? %>
              Ranked by the time of the examples that declared
              <code><%= @spec_file_durations.layer %></code> as their layer in their own
              <code>@intent</code> (never inferred from the path): every figure on this panel — each
              file's total, its examples timed, the file count — is that layer's alone, so a file
              appears here only if at least one of its examples declared it.
            <% end %>
            <% if @spec_file_durations.complete? %>
              Every example in every file listed reported a duration, so each total covers the
              whole of its file.
            <% else %>
              The "Examples timed" column is what each total was summed over: a file whose examples
              did not all report a duration has a total covering only the ones that did, and a file
              that reported none has no total to state rather than a zero. An example that never
              ran has no duration to report, so a missing timing is a faithful record rather than a
              gap.
            <% end %>
            The "Declared layers" column is how many of each listed file's examples declared each
            layer in their own <code>@intent</code>, counted over every example the run recorded in
            that file. "Undeclared" is the examples that declared no layer — never a layer inferred
            from the path.
            Counted off the rows this run wrote here, which is a different figure from the suite
            size on the Summary at the top of this page and may legitimately differ from it.
          <% end %>
          <% if @spec_file_durations.layer? %>
            <p class="text-xs mb-3" id="spec-file-durations-clear-layer">
              <%= link_to "Clear layer filter",
                          drill_down_path(@repository, layer: nil, anchor: "spec-file-durations"),
                          class: "rc-link" %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
          <%= render UI::TableComponent.new(
                columns: ["Spec file", { label: "Examples timed", end: true }, { label: "Total duration", end: true }, "Declared layers"],
                describedby: "spec-file-durations-basis", sortable: true) do %>
            <% @spec_file_durations.rows.each do |file| %>
              <%= drawer_row(file.path, kind: "Spec file", title: file.path,
                    facts: [["Total duration", file.duration_label], ["Examples timed", file.coverage_label],
                            ["Declared layers", file.layer_counts_label]],
                    body: layers_stack(file.layer_counts),
                    actions: [["Examples in this file", drill_down_path(@repository, spec_file: file.path, anchor: "slow"), :primary],
                              ["Unannotated here", drill_down_path(@repository, spec_file: file.path, anchor: "annotations"), :secondary],
                              ["Open on GitHub", "#{@repository.github_url}/blob/#{@latest_test_run.commit_sha}/#{file.path}", :ghost]]) do %>
                <td><%= row_open(file.path, mono: true, current: file.path == @spec_file_request) %></td>
                <td class="num mute" data-sort="<%= file.timed_count %>"><%= file.coverage_label %></td>
                <td class="num" data-sort="<%= file.total_seconds %>"><%= file.duration_label %></td>
                <td data-sort="<%= file.layer_counts.values.sum %>"><%= layers_stack(file.layer_counts) || tag.span("—", class: "text-app-content-secondary") %></td>
              <% end %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
          <% if @spec_file_durations.truncated? &&
                @spec_file_durations.rows.size < RequestedLimitParam::MAX_LIMIT %>
            <p class="text-xs mt-2">
              <%= link_to "Show up to #{number_with_delimiter(RequestedLimitParam::MAX_LIMIT)} heaviest files",
                          drill_down_path(@repository, limit: RequestedLimitParam::MAX_LIMIT,
                                          anchor: "spec-file-durations"),
                          class: "rc-link" %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
          <% if @limit_request %>
            <p class="text-xs mt-2">
              <%= link_to "Back to the #{SpecObservation::HEAVIEST_FILES_LIMIT} heaviest",
                          drill_down_path(@repository, limit: nil, anchor: "spec-file-durations"),
                          class: "rc-link" %>
            </p>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
                title: "No timings on this run",
                description: (@spec_file_durations.layer? ? "This run recorded #{@spec_file_durations.layer}-layer examples in " : "This run recorded examples in ") + \
                             "#{number_with_delimiter(@spec_file_durations.file_count)} " \
                             "#{'file'.pluralize(@spec_file_durations.file_count)} and a duration " \
                             "for none of them, so there is no wall clock to attribute to any " \
                             "file. An example that never ran reports no duration."
              ) %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
